  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mitigating the impact of conflict escalation in Lebanon on social, economic, and institutional stability &#x2013; Crisis Response and Stabilization programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lebanon is experiencing its most severe conflict escalation since the 2006 war, with a death toll exceeding 3,002, over 13,490 wounded, and more than 1.2 million people displaced, including over 191,800 being hosted in more that 1,135 collective shelters (4 November 2024). The latest wave of violence has profoundly affected the people of Lebanon, deepening the cycle of instability and conflict while severely impacting the country&#x2019;s institutional and economic stability, with long-term consequence</narrative>
  </description>
